WEBVTT

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.200
My brother and I were born
without any power.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.120
We were duds.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.920
Alice? Alice!

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.470
What the--?

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.810
Alice...

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:46.440
Karen is trying to change Alice's fate
by altering the past.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.820
What if we try to shut down
Togetsu's control computer, BABE?

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.450
Their Red Strings research
and plan implementation data

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.700
is all on BABE.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.210
Yuito, I need to talk to you
before we go to Togetsu.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.630
Me?

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:08.420
Not here. Let's step outside.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.180
You guys might as well hear this, too.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.800
What did you want to say?

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:23.560
It's about your father,
Chairman Joe Sumeragi.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.690
My dad?

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:29.190
I know who killed him.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:30.320
It was me.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.820
Huh?

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.200
Kagero.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:47.670
Kagero, this is no time for bad jokes.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.840
No, I don't think it's a joke.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.970
Kagero.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:36.230
Kagero's Confession

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:36.150
What are you talking about?

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:41.780
I told you before.
I was spying for Togetsu.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:46.120
Chairman Sumeragi didn't trust Togetsu.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.710
But even he hadn't discovered
their plan for using the Red Strings.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:54.420
However, he knew
they were up to something.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.720
So Togetsu saw him as a threat.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.640
Exactly. And that's why
they sent me to Suoh.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:07.850
I joined the OSF and waited for my chance.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:11.520
I thought you wanted to stop Togetsu.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:18.030
I did. And that's why I couldn't give them
any reason to suspect me.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.780
That meant I had to obey their orders.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.120
I have no beef with the chairman.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.240
It was for my own self-interest.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.080
Simply put,

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.290
I guess you could say
it was self-preservation.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.170
Hold on. What are you even talking about?

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.420
Kasane.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.710
You were there, right?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.760
I know what the chairman said to you.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:43.800
"The Others Suppression Force...
That was..."

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.970
He was trying to say Togetsu
had a spy in the OSF.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.640
And that spy was me.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:56.860
After that, the chairman said,
"Forget about me. Save yourself."

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.740
Th-The Others Suppression Force...

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.950
That was Toge...

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.910
Forget about me. Save yourself.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.290
Yes, he did say that.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.370
Then Yuito showed up.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.250
That means...

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.090
...Kagero really did do it.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.590
Do you understand now?

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.590
You're serious?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.970
You really--

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:27.060
I already told you I did.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:30.730
Why are you just telling me this now?

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:36.110
Does the reason really matter?
I just thought I should apologize.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:39.610
Of course, I know you can't forgive me.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.440
So, what now?

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.360
I'll leave if you want me gone.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.330
So that's how you handle things?

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.500
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:53.620
After all, that's just the kinda guy I am.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:57.920
Then allow me to finish this my way.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.130
Yuito?!

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:01.800
Whoa, I didn't see this coming.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:05.260
You're not serious, are you,
Mr. Goody Two-shoes?

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.560
We're really gonna do this?!

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.180
Say your prayers, Kagero!

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.980
I'm serious. Deadly serious.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:18.190
Stop this! Yuito! Kagero!

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.940
Leave them be.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.070
Why?!

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:25.780
They can't move past this until
they get it out of their systems.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.160
This is ridiculous.
Wake me up when it's over.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:37.040
He's serious? What does a naive,
rich boy know about such things?!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.460
Like that's even possible!

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.320
Shit!

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.790
Give a guy some time to think!

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:18.750
Yuito. You've grown that powerful?!

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:27.880
He's really trying to kill me.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.440
This has gone too far.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.570
I can't die yet.

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.780
Wait. Yuito!

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.160
Please don't kill me!

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.740
Shit!

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:54.160
Wait! Yuito!

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:57.290
I-If I die here...

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:02.170
...all I've done for her the past
2,000 years will have been in vain!

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:17.520
I finally got the truth
out of you, Kagero.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:21.980
W-Wait. What? Are you telling me...

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:30.200
That was the only way to get you
to speak from the heart.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:32.740
You've got to be kidding me...

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:35.700
But there's more, isn't there?

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.490
Over here!

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:43.080
...I await you! Join me here in Seiran!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:47.460
Together we shall crush
the New Himukan regime!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.140
Who are you?

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.110
Oh, you're with the OSF.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.190
Am I glad you're here.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.360
You have my thanks.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:14.120
Sorry, but I don't think
you'll wanna thank me,

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:17.120
Chairman Joe Sumeragi.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:21.000
You're with the rebels.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.290
Wrong.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:26.380
But Seiran did give me this chance
by attacking Suoh.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:29.050
I must thank Karen and the rebel forces.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.170
Now I see. Togetsu.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.800
You got that one right.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:36.550
If you came to kill me,
why did you just save me?

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.520
I have my reasons.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.440
I'm gonna report back that I killed you.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.850
I want you to lay low for a while.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.400
I can offer a safe place.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.990
You're going to betray Togetsu? Why?

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:54.860
Like I said, I have my reasons.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.950
So what will it be?

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.120
I won't hide.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.540
New Himuka is descending into chaos.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:07.090
I can't abandon its people.
I'm a member of the Sumeragi family.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:12.470
Even if I don't off you here, Togetsu
won't ever stop hunting you down.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:16.140
The Sumeragis have two fine sons.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:19.850
The OSF's promising rookie,
Yuito Sumeragi,

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:22.560
and its chief, Kaito Sumeragi.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:26.770
Why not let them handle things
so you can enjoy some R&R?

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:33.950
You know as well as I do what
the Sumeragi family came here to do.

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:36.200
Yuito is still in the dark

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.160
about this nation and the Sumeragi family.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:43.710
And Kaito misunderstands
the true will of Yakumo Sumeragi.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:48.080
Yakumo did not seek the path of violence.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:52.420
He would've never allowed
the Sumeragi family and New Himuka

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:55.760
to do what they have done to its people,

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:59.640
even if it was to protect
a peaceful way of life.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:06.650
That is why I must not hide
nor die here this day.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:08.900
I must save this nation from its doom

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:14.610
and make my sons understand how to
right the wrongs that have been done.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.820
Well, now. You're not as bad as I thought.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.450
You're just like your ancestors.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:27.210
It's even harder to kill you
when you say stuff like that.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:28.540
However,

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.170
if you refuse to come with me...

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.840
Stand back!

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:48.140
Damn you!

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.320
Shit!

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.290
Chairman Sumeragi!

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.790
Hang in there, Mr. Chairman.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:15.670
So my father was trying
to right this nation's wrongs.

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:20.050
I never laid hands on him.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:25.020
But by confronting him like that,
it's as if...

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.850
...I'd killed him myself.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:32.520
So you wanted to settle this matter
before returning to Togetsu?

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:36.070
You were trying to provoke Yuito?

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:41.740
I knew Yuito would have to respond.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:45.790
But at the last moment,
I realized what was important to me.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:47.870
I didn't want to die.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.790
I knew I couldn't die yet,

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.630
at least not till I
thwarted Togetsu's plan.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.760
Thanks, my dear Tsugumi.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:02.470
Who'd you mean when you said,
"All I've done for her"?

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:06.970
Back in Togetsu, you said you
left your family on the moon.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.640
By "her," did you mean...

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.560
Yeah, my daughter.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:16.070
I left a wife and daughter on the Moon.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:19.990
If history is rewound,
our daughter will cease to exist.

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:22.950
I will <i>not </i>let that happen.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:27.120
We cannot let Togetsu use the Red Strings.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.370
But 2,000 years have passed.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.040
My family will have been
laid to rest ages ago.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.090
So you probably think
I'm acting like an idiot.

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:38.050
But my wife and my child did exist.

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:41.590
I won't let them be erased from history.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:48.560
As the head of state, my father was
at the center of what went wrong.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:54.650
What happened to Nagi and Naomi
can probably be traced back to him.

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:59.650
Despite that, he is
the only father I've ever had.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:07.660
That's why I understand how you don't
want your family to be erased.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:10.790
As Arahabaki stole my past from me,

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.660
I was terrified.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:16.670
It felt like I was losing myself.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:20.300
I can't let anyone else suffer
that same feeling.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:26.680
Erasing somebody's past is a crime
that should never be forgiven.

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:30.810
Let's stop Togetsu.

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:33.390
This doesn't mean I forgive you.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:39.190
But together, I believe we can
stand up to Togetsu's threat.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:45.700
You're way more mature than I am.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:50.160
Or maybe it's just I'm
a perpetual manchild.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:55.670
Looks like you've decided
the matter for this old sad-sack.

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:57.130
Yuito.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:15:01.500
Allow me to help you stop Togetsu.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.710
You got it!

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.450
The shaking subsided.

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:38.170
That didn't quite feel
like a normal quake.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:42.880
Didn't it remind you of the earthquake
on the Kunad Highway?

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.350
Everyone all right?

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:56.180
The Kunad Gate just experienced
a momentary data anomaly.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:59.230
Powerful shaking was felt
across all of New Himuka.

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:01.860
But there doesn't seem
to be any major damage.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:07.280
We're okay, too. There are no signs
of landslides here on Hieno Mountain.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:10.160
Does this mean the Kunad Gate is growing?

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:16.660
It is my power that sustains it.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.620
The gate would vanish if I died.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:23.710
That was the only way to stop it.

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:28.970
So it's my power that feeds it.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:37.390
Togetsu must be studying
the Kunad Gate, too, right?

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:43.730
Yes. While we're shutting BABE down,
let's collect all the data we can.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:47.030
We just might find something useful.

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:48.860
Yuito.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:51.660
How has your power been lately?

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:52.950
What?

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:56.120
Have you felt like
something wasn't quite right?

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.160
No, nothing like that.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:03.000
After you guys saved me from Arahabaki,
I haven't had headaches or anything.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.000
I wonder why.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.050
That's good to hear.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:09.760
But when I was fighting you,
how can I put this?

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.510
It was like I felt
a massive surge of power.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:26.320
Maybe it was just
your emotions in high gear.

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:28.650
You think that might explain it?

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:34.070
It's true that emotions
can affect psionic powers.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:37.040
But if that wasn't the case...

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:43.040
Another explanation is it's
a sign you're losing your power.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:48.050
Some say waning power will be
temporarily enhanced to an abnormal level.

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.510
My power is going to disappear?

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:56.390
It's an extremely rare phenomenon
that occurs as the brain ages.

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:58.970
If this is going to happen to you now...

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:04.520
Your brain has already
sustained heavy damage.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:09.780
Then there's the fact
that I was once a dud.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.070
What do you mean?

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:14.110
You were a dud?

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:20.500
You became a psionics user
after they experimented on you?

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:23.000
Were you really a dud?

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.210
You sure there wasn't
some sort of mistake?

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:27.250
I wasn't even sure myself.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:30.170
But after hearing Karen and Luka's story,

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:33.260
I realized I was probably
just like they were.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:37.180
I'd say it's more than likely.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:43.600
How long do you think my power will last?

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:46.610
Will I start losing it today or tomorrow?

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:49.320
It's not supposed to happen that fast.

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:53.150
But it's hard to say.
There are so few cases like yours.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:56.660
It's not a foregone conclusion, is it?

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:58.950
It's all speculation.

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:01.950
You're right.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.920
Let's just get to Togetsu
as fast as we can.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.000
Got it.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:10.590
Then I'll go on ahead
and pave the way for your arrival.

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:12.880
Okay, I'm counting on you.

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:30.020
It's open.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.190
Let's go.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.080
Hurry!

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:44.660
They must already know we're here!

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.710
Let's make a beeline for BABE.

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:49.040
They're here!

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.970
This is quite the welcome!

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:56.590
We'll break through!

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:10.940
Yuito! Kasane!

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:18.490
It seems they want
your brains at all costs.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.410
I'll teleport us!

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:25.620
Gather here!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:26.580
Luka!

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.830
You'll take us straight to BABE?!

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:32.000
Isn't that risky?!

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:35.760
I verified this building's structure
the last time we were here.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:40.340
Once we get near BABE,
they'll have to tone down their attacks.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:42.640
Yuito, hurry!

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:44.680
Coming!

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.850
Luka, do it!

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.270
Here goes!

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:54.520
Yuito!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:16.170
Looks like we made it
to BABE in one piece.

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:20.260
It worked.

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:22.340
Are you okay?

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.720
Shouldn't you rest for a bit?

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:27.720
No, but I appreciate the thought.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.520
Let's hurry.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:32.440
Hey, Haruka! Wataru!

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:35.190
Psynet is being blocked
just like last time.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.570
That's right.

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:42.610
The shaking is even worse now.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.490
Is this from the Kunad Gate again?

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.540
We better hurry.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.420
Please wait.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:04.140
Please listen to me.

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:07.890
That voice...

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:09.430
It can't be.

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:18.020
Please listen to me.

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:18.980
--Mother!
--Mom!

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.150
Huh?

00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:41.720
<i>I've been a prisoner</i>
<i>of my own longing</i>

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:51.350
<i>The shimmering heat signals me to halt</i>

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:53.480
<i>There's a stranger in me</i>

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:55.980
<i>I'll fly high so I won't be scared</i>

00:22:55.980 --> 00:23:01.230
<i>By this new self I've never seen</i>

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:03.030
<i>I'm spreading my wings</i>

00:23:03.030 --> 00:23:05.360
<i>Bird in florid flight</i>

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:10.080
<i>Lift your eyes to the scarlet sky</i>

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:15.290
<i>Overtaken by the mighty wind</i>

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:20.460
<i>The view unfolds upon a world</i>
<i>that begins turning</i>

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:24.930
<i>Amid the intermingling light</i>

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:30.810
<i>I keep searching for tomorrow</i>

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:32.430
<i>Tomorrow's in your hands</i>

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:35.640
<i>Don't tell me now you're afraid</i>

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:37.270
<i>There's no time to waste</i>

00:23:37.270 --> 00:23:40.230
<i>Keep going forward</i>

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:44.570
<i>There's nothing to be afraid of</i>

00:23:44.570 --> 00:23:46.240
<i>Now, let's go</i>

00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:51.700
<i>Into a brand-new day</i>

00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:11.930
Together Again
